WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.034
-I'm so happy that you're here.

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:04.637
-Me too. Very excited.
-I'm a fan.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.238
It's your first time
on our show.

00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:08.641
-Yes.
-I want to get to know you.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.277
I want to ask you -- you're
from Cuba, is that correct?

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.613
-Yeah.
-And did you start acting there?

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:14.748
-I did.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:17.516
I went to drama school
when I was 14.

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:20.520
That was like, four years
of theater school.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.921
-Yeah.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:25.091
-And when I was on my second
year, I did my first movie.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.592
I auditioned for it
and I got it,

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.595
and the teachers
were not very happy

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:31.130
and they told me
if I did the movie,

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.798
I was going to --
[ Clicks tongue ]

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:34.900
get kicked out of school.
-Of acting school?

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.436
-Yeah, because, you know...
-Wait.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:37.903
This is kind of the goal, right?

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:39.072
-Well, if you do a movie,
you're not going to school.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.973
So...
-I understand, yeah.

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:43.576
-I still did it, though.
-That's right.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.712
Look at you now.
Come on. Yeah, exactly right.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.646
[ Applause ]

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:50.215
-So they made me repeat
the year.

00:00:50.215 --> 00:00:51.417
-Oh, really? They did?

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:52.418
-It was worth it.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:53.886
-Yeah. Oh, good. Yeah.

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:57.323
I also heard something that you
used to hitchhike to school.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.724
-Yeah. Didn't you?

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:00.693
-No. No. That's very dangerous.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:01.694
I don't hitchhike.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.128
-No, it's not in Cuba.

00:01:03.128 --> 00:01:06.966
I mean, you just get there
faster than just --

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.434
-I understand, yeah, but...

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:09.802
-I will get there faster
than you, maybe.

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:10.870
-Yes, you will. Yeah.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.205
Because no one
would pick me up.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.640
If we're both on the street
with our thumb out,

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.742
they're gonna pick you up
and not me.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.109
-Well, I didn't
do the thumb thing.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:20.780
I'd just go to the stoplight,
so the cars have to stop.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.448
-You would just jump
into strangers' cars,

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:24.017
like, "Take me to school"?

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.385
-Pretty much.
-Yeah?

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:27.286
-You just go to the window.

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:28.854
I'm like, "Hey, can you go
to the next stoplight?"

00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:31.824
-No, this is too dangerous.
Oh, no, no.

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.726
-No, it's not. I mean,
everyone's very used to it.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:36.462
It's like free carpool.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.498
[ Laughter ]
So.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:42.235
-Any children watching,
don't do this.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:46.706
But is that how you
ended up in the Bond movie?

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.507
Because you're from --
No, no, no! Not hitchhiking.

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:49.842
No, not hitchhiking.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.177
Being from Cuba, sorry.
-"Hey."

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.879
-"Hi, do you guys mind
if I'm in this movie?"

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.647
-"Do you go to London?"

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.983
-"Can I be in the new
007 movie?"

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.218
"Sure. Come on."

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:00.019
No, but is it
because you're from Cuba?

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.621
Is that how?

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:05.457
-I mean, something
to do with that.

00:02:05.457 --> 00:02:07.527
I think...

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:08.861
-You're so good in this,
by the way.

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:10.763
I told you backstage,
but I really mean it.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.699
-Thank you.
-You get a giant laugh.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:14.133
I'm not going to spoil
anything for anyone.

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:16.836
I won't ever do that.
But, dude.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.706
This one scene,
it's just beautiful to look at.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.039
I go, it's iconic.

00:02:21.039 --> 00:02:22.441
-Thank you very much.
-What you did, you crushed it.

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:23.509
You're fantastic.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:25.411
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.947
-Do you want to describe
who you play? Your 00 agent?

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:32.952
-Yeah, I play Paloma.
She's a CIA agent in Cuba.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:37.423
She's there to assist Bond
in his mission.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:40.159
And she very excited
about the job.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:43.263
-Yeah, yeah. You really are.
-She's very, very happy,

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:45.031
and like, you know, also nervous

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.767
because it's her first job,
big, big job.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:51.003
-Yeah, you're like --
I could say the line.

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:52.137
-What line?
-You're like, "Oh,

00:02:52.137 --> 00:02:53.506
I'm only three weeks
in training on the job."

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.875
-Yeah, yeah, exactly.
-Yeah.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.910
-The funny thing is that
I also had only

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.313
three weeks' training, so.

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:02.081
[ Laughter ]
I think I just kept saying it

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:06.486
so much that Cary was like,
"Just say it. It's fine."

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:09.088
-Oh, because that's real life.
-"Just keep it."

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.391
-You just came from doing
a Marilyn Monroe movie

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:13.425
right to this.
-Yeah.

00:03:13.425 --> 00:03:17.463
-Was that difficult, to go
from that extreme to this?

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:20.399
-Yeah. Well...yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:24.136
-I mean,
Marilyn did not train at all.

00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:26.506
-No. Yeah, no.
-Like Paloma.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:31.577
I mean, it was, it's like
opposite things, you know?

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:33.946
I did Marilyn,
it was very intense,

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:36.749
and then I finished shooting
on a Friday.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.351
I got on a plane on a Saturday

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.954
and I started shooting Bond
on Monday.

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:44.423
So I just remember
being on set like,

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:47.526
my first scene and I kind of
like started whispering

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:49.361
and Cary was like, "Mmm.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:51.730
No, we're here now."

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.800
-"You're in this movie now."
-This movie now.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.401
-[ As Marilyn Monroe ]
"Happy birthday."

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.603
"No, we're not doing that now.
We're doing this."

00:03:57.603 --> 00:04:00.340
-Kind of.
-We're doing this movie now.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.042
Daniel Craig.
You guys are great together.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.544
Is it odd that
you were in "Knives Out"

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:08.080
and then you're with Bond?

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.882
You guys are
a traveling team now.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.051
-[ Laughing ]
-You go together.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.652
-Yeah, that was awesome.

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:17.389
I mean, "Knives Out,"
it was such a special movie.

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:18.590
We had so much fun,

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:21.260
and Daniel and I
were together all the time.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.495
We were this team.

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.296
But back then,

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:26.665
only Daniel was talking
about Bond and his training.

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:28.934
I had no idea what was
going to happen.

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:29.969
-That you were gonna be in it?
-No, no.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:32.037
That happened,
like, four months later.

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:33.072
-He's phenomenal, man.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:35.641
-It was a very happy
coincidence.

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:37.110
-I loved the movie
top to bottom.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.510
I'm a big fan of all the movies,

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:40.780
but this one has everything
you could even think about.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.015
Action, you know,

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:45.551
suspense, spy thriller thing,
love story.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:46.953
-Humor.
-Humor.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:50.623
It's emotional,
but also it's real stunts.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:54.059
It's not just like a CGI thing,
which, you know, is fine.

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:57.296
This is like, real
human beings doing crazy stunts.

00:04:57.296 --> 00:04:58.697
You're like, "What?"

00:04:58.697 --> 00:05:01.067
I've never seen anything like
that one motorcycle thing.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.101
-It is spectacular, really.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.602
-It's a movie.

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:06.372
It's just like, wow, they made
an unbelievable movie.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.840
-You really like it.
-I loved it.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.374
I loved it. You were so good.

00:05:09.374 --> 00:05:11.243
I want to show everyone
a clip from the movie.

00:05:11.243 --> 00:05:14.180
Here's Ana de Armas in
"No Time to Die." Take a look.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.348
♪♪

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:16.449
[ Gunfire ]

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:26.358 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:36.368 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:45.077 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:45.077 --> 00:05:46.946
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:48.981
That's what I'm talking about!

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.717
That is what I'm talking about!
That exact scene!

00:05:51.717 --> 00:05:54.286
You're amazing.
Ana de Armas!

00:05:54.286 --> 00:05:57.089
Here's how it works.
We have nine mystery boxes

00:05:57.089 --> 00:05:59.425
containing objects
no one has ever seen before.

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:02.027
On your turn, you pick a box,
take out an object,

00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:03.562
and describe it
to your opponent.

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:05.230
Then they have to guess
if you're lying

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:06.498
or telling the truth.

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:07.733
We'll play three rounds.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:09.101
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:09.101 --> 00:06:11.804
[ Deep voice ] Ana, why don't
you pick the first box?

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:12.871
-Of course.

00:06:12.871 --> 00:06:14.006
-Number 5!
-Oh.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:15.474
-8!
-5!

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:17.910
[ Audience shouting ]

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.812
-I can't hear anything.
-No, you can't hear.

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:21.013
Now they're yelling
every number.

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:22.647
Yeah, they're just...

00:06:22.647 --> 00:06:26.719
[ Audience shouting ]

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:28.587
Yeah. They li-- 5's a --

00:06:28.587 --> 00:06:30.656
Okay. Oh, this could be acting
right now.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:31.690
I don't know if it's heavy.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:33.059
-Doing this with heels
is not good.

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.660
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.595
-Alright. Now, you open it,
and then you place it out here

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:38.030
so that the audience can see.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:41.266
And the lying begins now --
or the truth telling begins now.

00:06:41.266 --> 00:06:45.304
Here's where the game becomes...
-Okay.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:47.239
-...exciting.
-Okay.

00:06:47.239 --> 00:06:49.709
[ Light laughter ]
What?

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:53.279
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:53.279 --> 00:06:55.014
This is very creepy.
Don't look.

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:56.114
[ Laughter ]
-I'm not looking.

00:06:56.114 --> 00:06:58.384
I can't see it.

00:06:58.384 --> 00:07:00.619
-Who thinks of these things?

00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:02.387
-Wha-- Who thinks --
are you asking --

00:07:02.387 --> 00:07:04.857
Yeah. Okay.
-What to put in these boxes?

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:05.858
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:06.892
-All right.
Describe, describe.

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:09.094
-Wow.
-What?

00:07:09.094 --> 00:07:13.332
What is in --
What is in box number 5?

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:16.535
-Oh, my gosh.
So...this is a --

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:18.004
-You're lying.

00:07:18.004 --> 00:07:21.440
[ Laughter ]

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.542
Oh, wait.

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:24.943
-The -- So maybe
I don't know how to say

00:07:24.943 --> 00:07:26.812
something in English, so...
-Okay.

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:27.980
-You know.
-Okay.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.548
-Is it "pumpkin"?

00:07:29.548 --> 00:07:31.417
-Okay, that sounds about right.

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:32.918
Topical.
-Okay.

00:07:32.918 --> 00:07:39.758
With three people taking --
it's like a Jacuzzi pumpkin.

00:07:39.758 --> 00:07:44.363
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:45.931
-I just want to hear you say
"Jacuzzi pumpkin,"

00:07:45.931 --> 00:07:47.265
like, forever, like...

00:07:47.265 --> 00:07:48.667
"It's a Jacuzzi pumpkin."

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:49.835
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:07:49.835 --> 00:07:51.303
[ Both laugh ]
-Okay.

00:07:51.303 --> 00:07:52.404
-Gonna get better.
-Alright.

00:07:52.404 --> 00:07:54.573
So, is there three people
in the pumpkin?

00:07:54.573 --> 00:07:57.843
[ Laughter ]

00:07:57.843 --> 00:07:59.512 line:0%
♪♪

